course: dictionary
lesson: 9435
title: Stain: a mark that will not come out
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A stain is a dirty mark or spot that is hard to remove. «Paint stains clothes, so you wear an old shirt or apron.» Here stains is a verb: paint makes marks that are hard to get out, so you protect your clothes.
explain: Stain can also be a noun. «A grass stain» is the mark itself, the green spot left on your knee after a football match. Look at the words around the word to see which job it does in the sentence.
explain: Stain has a second meaning too: a dye used to colour wood, or to make cells easy to see under a microscope. Scientists use a stain so they can see the tiny parts of a cell clearly. The context tells you which meaning is right.
fact: A stain is a dirty mark or spot that is hard to remove.
fact: «Stain» can be a noun (a stain) or a verb (to stain, stains, stained, staining).
fact: Quick cold water helps when you treat a stain, and washing brushes straight away stops paint drying hard.
fact: Teachers use a stain, like iodine, to colour cells so they can be seen under a microscope.
fact: «Stained glass» is glass with coloured patterns, and «stained with» means marked with something, such as «stained with ink».
exercise: «Paint stains clothes, so you wear an old shirt or apron.» What does stains mean here? | Smells strong | Dries quickly | *Makes marks that are hard to remove | Washes clean
exercise: «Evidence like a stain usually stays behind after an accident.» What does stain mean here? | *A mark left behind | A loud noise | A piece of cloth | A happy memory
exercise: Priya's teacher uses a stain under the microscope. What is a stain used for in science? | To wash cells clean | To hide cells from view | To make cells bigger than they really are | *To colour cells so they can be seen clearly
test: What job does stain do in «The grass stain on his knee would not come out»? | *A noun, the mark itself | A verb, an action | A question word | A number
test: Which sentence uses stain to mean a dye? | *«The teacher used a stain to colour the cells» | «The shirt has a stain on the collar» | «Washing powder helps remove a stain» | «The ink stain spread across the page»
exam: Which meaning fits «The biologist used iodine as a stain so the cells showed up clearly»? | A shiny coat of paint on a wall | A dirty mark that is hard to remove | To wash clothes until they are clean | *A dye that makes cells easy to see
